SUMMARY:Distinguished lecture: DOE Under Secretary for Science Darío Gil

X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><base href="https://inl.sharepoint.com" /></head><body><p><strong>Distinguished lecture: DOE Under Secretary for Science Darío Gil to speak Aug. 3</strong></p><p><span class="fontSizeMedium"><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">U.S. Department of Energy Under Secretary for Science Darío Gil is the next speaker in our Distinguished Lecture in Science, Technology and Policy series. The series invites prestigious researchers, policymakers and thought leaders to the laboratory to engage with our world-class staff members.</span></span><br /><br /><span class="fontSizeMedium"><span style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);color:rgb(51, 51, 51);">Gil oversees the department's Office of Science, the nation's largest federal sponsor of basic research in the physical sciences, and provides leadership for the department's 17 national laboratories. He serves as DOE's principal advisor on science and technology, guiding research and innovation in areas including artificial intelligence, advanced computing, quantum information science, fusion energy, nuclear physics and high-performance computing. Gil previously led IBM Research, one of the world's largest corporate research organizations. He is recognized internationally for advancing emerging technologies.</span></span></p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);">A fireside-chat-style Q&amp;A session will follow Gil's remarks. The event closes with a poster session and reception that is open to all.</p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);">Please join us for this opportunity.</p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);margin-left:40px;"><strong>When: </strong>Monday, Aug. 3, 3:30 to 5 p.m.</p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);margin-left:40px;"><strong>Where: </strong>INL Meeting Center, Room A102</p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);margin-left:40px;"><a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https://contactmonkey.com/api/v1/tracker?cm_session%3Daf4627ef-86c6-4f08-a06a-f4cd0b38fd96%26cs%3Dbd1668fc-ad06-4aa9-bb4a-ba8d9643e124%26i%3D3b92179f035bbc3f84562e96591ee996bee89a775%26cls%3Dcd66b9fd-6f29-4437-84ad-129b6df87c53%26cm_type%3Dlink%26cm_link%3Da6438fd4-717c-4f86-a2c4-8ecace3e1509%26cm_destination%3Dhttps://inl.sharepoint.com/:b:/r/sites/iHome/Shared%2520Documents/22-50478_Gil_flyer_R0.pdf?csf%3D1%26web%3D1%26e%3DGO04KL&amp;data=05%7c02%7cMike.Sponseller%40inl.gov%7c0dc9331a516944f82bcd08deee7a2a52%7c4cf464b7869a42368da2a98566485554%7c0%7c0%7c639210405875973229%7cUnknown%7cTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7c0%7c%7c%7c&amp;sdata=pJnTM7FzUE31DKLdoAZA5OJpvTjMPHDUZzirPpxGQqQ%3D&amp;reserved=0"><u>Flyer</u></a></p><p style="background-color:rgb(255, 255, 255);">This event is in-person only. A recording will be available for employees unable to attend. Recordings of distinguished lectures are available on the <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https://contactmonkey.com/api/v1/tracker?cm_session%3Daf4627ef-86c6-4f08-a06a-f4cd0b38fd96%26cs%3Dbd1668fc-ad06-4aa9-bb4a-ba8d9643e124%26i%3D3e5b0499cb4f0d998298aee4a6263f6418fbacd3e%26cls%3De0e3210e-17eb-4e4b-ba7c-a8300be86b72%26cm_type%3Dlink%26cm_link%3D75e7cc19-b4b5-401b-b834-592b05fd14b8%26cm_destination%3Dhttps://inl.sharepoint.com/sites/LaboratoryDirector/SitePages/Presentation-Library.aspx%23recorded-presentations-director-s-distinguished-lecture-series-in-science%252C-technology%252C-and-policy&amp;data=05%7c02%7cMike.Sponseller%40inl.gov%7c0dc9331a516944f82bcd08deee7a2a52%7c4cf464b7869a42368da2a98566485554%7c0%7c0%7c639210405875995971%7cUnknown%7cTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7c0%7c%7c%7c&amp;sdata=F5xfPBp11piOrXL0pdoj5bNP2rlFECKY68Y6E0EPrso%3D&amp;reserved=0"><u>Laboratory Director's website</u></a>.</p></body></html>






